 "body": "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/css/article-tables.css\"><p>A $40 gasket set can shut down a filling line. On an ABC report it sits at the very bottom of class C, next to the drive belts, and gets the least attention of anything in the plant.</p>\n<p>That is the problem with applying standard ABC analysis in a factory. The method in <a href=\"abc-inventory-analysis.html\">Post&nbsp;1</a> ranks items by annual dollar usage, and for a distributor that works well: when an item runs out, you lose that item's sales. In a plant, running out of one input can stop everything that depends on it. The cost of a stockout has little to do with the price of the part.</p>\n<p>This post keeps the ABC method and adds one thing to it: a criticality rating. If you have not read <a href=\"abc-inventory-analysis.html\">Post&nbsp;1</a>, start there for the five steps. Here we cover only what changes for a manufacturer.</p>\n<h2>Three pools of inventory, three behaviours</h2>\n<p>A distributor holds one kind of inventory: finished goods for sale. A manufacturer holds several, and each follows different rules.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Pool</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">What drives its demand</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">What a stockout costs</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">How to classify it</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Raw materials and packaging</td><td>The production schedule. Usage follows what you plan to make.</td><td>A delayed or cancelled batch, idle labour, late customer orders</td><td>ABC by annual value consumed, plus criticality</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Spare parts and maintenance supplies</td><td>Equipment wear and failure. Usage is low and irregular.</td><td>Downtime on the equipment, and everything downstream of it</td><td>Criticality first; value is almost irrelevant</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Work in progress</td><td>Your own process and batch sizes</td><td>Rarely a stockout; the cost is cash and floor space</td><td>Leave out of ABC. Control it through scheduling.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Finished goods</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Customer orders</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A lost or late sale</td><td>Standard ABC by sales, as in <a href=\"abc-inventory-analysis.html\">Post&nbsp;1</a></td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Two practical points follow. First, use <strong>consumption</strong>, the quantity issued to production or maintenance, not purchases. Purchases reflect when you bought, not what you used. Second, keep the unit of measure consistent. If resin is bought by the drum and issued by the kilogram, convert before you multiply.</p>\n<h2>A worked example: a coatings manufacturer</h2>\n<p>Ridgeline Coatings is a fictional maker of industrial coatings. The list below covers 20 purchased items across raw materials, packaging and spare parts, with a combined annual usage of $2,420,750. It is ranked exactly as in <a href=\"abc-inventory-analysis.html\">Post&nbsp;1</a>, with cut-offs at 80% and 95% of cumulative value.</p>\n<table class=\"t-wide\">\n<tr><th>Rank</th><th>Item</th><th>Pool</th><th>Annual usage</th><th>Unit cost</th><th>Annual value</th><th>Cumulative %</th><th>Class</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">1</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">RM-01 Epoxy resin</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">180,000&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$4.20</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$756,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">31.2%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">2</td><td>RM-02 Titanium dioxide pigment</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">95,000&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$3.80</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$361,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">46.1%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">3</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">RM-03 Xylene solvent</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">210,000&nbsp;L</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$1.35</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$283,500</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">57.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">4</td><td>PK-01 20 L steel pail with lid</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Packaging</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">48,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$5.60</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$268,800</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">69.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">5</td><td>RM-04 Polyamine hardener</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">42,000&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$6.10</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$256,200</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">79.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">A</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">6</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">RM-05 Acrylic resin</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">38,000&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$3.50</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$133,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">85.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">7</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">PK-02 4 L can with lid</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Packaging</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">60,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$1.90</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$114,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">89.7%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">8</td><td>RM-06 Calcium carbonate extender</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">160,000&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$0.45</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$72,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">92.7%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">9</td><td>RM-07 Iron oxide red pigment</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">9,000&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$5.20</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$46,800</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">94.7%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">B</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">10</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">PK-04 Pallets</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Packaging</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">2,600</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$14.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$36,400</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">96.2%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">11</td><td>RM-08 Dispersant additive</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">2,400&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$14.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$33,600</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">97.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">12</td><td>RM-09 Defoamer additive</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">1,100&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$11.50</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$12,650</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">98.1%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">13</td><td>SP-03 Filter bags, box of 50</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Spare part</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">90</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$120.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$10,800</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">98.5%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">14</td><td>PK-03 Product labels, per 1,000</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Packaging</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">120</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$85.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$10,200</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">98.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">15</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">RM-10 Thickener</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Raw material</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">900&nbsp;kg</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$9.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$8,100</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.3%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">16</td><td>SP-01 Disperser mechanical seal</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Spare part</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">4</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$1,850.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$7,400</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.6%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">17</td><td>SP-04 Pump diaphragm kit</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Spare part</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">12</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$310.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$3,720</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.7%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">18</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">SP-06 Dispersion blade</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Spare part</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">6</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$480.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$2,880</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.8%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">19</td><td>SP-02 Filling line gasket set</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Spare part</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">60</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$40.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$2,400</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">99.9%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">20</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">SP-05 Drive belt</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Spare part</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">20</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$65.00</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">$1,300</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">100.0%</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">C</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>The split looks familiar: 5 A items carry 79.5% of the value, 4 B items carry 15.1%, and 11 C items carry 5.3%. By the usual logic, the plant would now manage five items closely and put the bottom eleven on autopilot.</p>\n<h2>What the value ranking misses</h2>\n<p>Now mark the items that would stop production if they ran out. The plant's production and maintenance leads identify six.</p>\n<figure style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><svg role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Pareto chart of 20 purchased items ranked by annual value, with the six vital items highlighted. Epoxy resin, titanium dioxide pigment and hardener are class A. The dispersant additive at $33,600 a year, the mechanical seal at $7,400 and the gasket set at $2,400 are all in class C.\" viewBox=\"0 0 720 400\" width=\"720\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;min-width:560px\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" font-family=\"Inter,system-ui,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><text x=\"58\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\">Three of the six line-stopping items sit in the C tail</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"46\" fill=\"#5A6475\">Bars: annual value per item, ranked. Line: cumulative share of the $2,420,750 total.</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"63\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\" font-weight=\"600\">Blue: vital items, where a stockout stops production.</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"330.0\" y2=\"330.0\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"334.0\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$0</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"255.3\" y2=\"255.3\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"259.3\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$250k</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"180.5\" y2=\"180.5\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"184.5\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$500k</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"105.8\" y2=\"105.8\" stroke=\"#E3E6EC\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"109.8\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$750k</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"149.2\" y2=\"149.2\" stroke=\"#8A93A3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"153.2\" fill=\"#5A6475\">80%</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"115.3\" y2=\"115.3\" stroke=\"#8A93A3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/><text x=\"660\" y=\"119.3\" fill=\"#5A6475\">95%</text><rect x=\"62.0\" y=\"104.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"226.0\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>RM-01 Epoxy resin: $756,000 a year, class A</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 76.9 344)\" x=\"76.9\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\" font-weight=\"600\">RM-01</text><rect x=\"91.8\" y=\"222.1\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"107.9\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>RM-02 Titanium dioxide pigment: $361,000 a year, class A</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 106.7 344)\" x=\"106.7\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\" font-weight=\"600\">RM-02</text><rect x=\"121.6\" y=\"245.2\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"84.8\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>RM-03 Xylene solvent: $283,500 a year, class A</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 136.5 344)\" x=\"136.5\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">RM-03</text><rect x=\"151.4\" y=\"249.6\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"80.4\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>PK-01 20 L steel pail with lid: $268,800 a year, class A</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 166.3 344)\" x=\"166.3\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">PK-01</text><rect x=\"181.2\" y=\"253.4\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"76.6\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>RM-04 Polyamine hardener: $256,200 a year, class A</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 196.1 344)\" x=\"196.1\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\" font-weight=\"600\">RM-04</text><rect x=\"211.0\" y=\"290.2\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"39.8\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>RM-05 Acrylic resin: $133,000 a year, class B</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 225.9 344)\" x=\"225.9\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">RM-05</text><rect x=\"240.8\" y=\"295.9\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"34.1\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>PK-02 4 L can with lid: $114,000 a year, class B</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 255.7 344)\" x=\"255.7\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">PK-02</text><rect x=\"270.6\" y=\"308.5\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"21.5\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>RM-06 Calcium carbonate extender: $72,000 a year, class B</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 285.5 344)\" x=\"285.5\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">RM-06</text><rect x=\"300.4\" y=\"316.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"14.0\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>RM-07 Iron oxide red pigment: $46,800 a year, class B</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 315.3 344)\" x=\"315.3\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">RM-07</text><rect x=\"330.2\" y=\"319.1\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"10.9\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>PK-04 Pallets: $36,400 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 345.1 344)\" x=\"345.1\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">PK-04</text><rect x=\"360.0\" y=\"320.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"10.0\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>RM-08 Dispersant additive: $33,600 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 374.9 344)\" x=\"374.9\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\" font-weight=\"600\">RM-08</text><rect x=\"389.8\" y=\"326.2\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"3.8\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>RM-09 Defoamer additive: $12,650 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 404.7 344)\" x=\"404.7\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">RM-09</text><rect x=\"419.6\" y=\"326.8\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"3.2\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>SP-03 Filter bags, box of 50: $10,800 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 434.5 344)\" x=\"434.5\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">SP-03</text><rect x=\"449.4\" y=\"327.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"3.0\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>PK-03 Product labels, per 1,000: $10,200 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 464.3 344)\" x=\"464.3\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">PK-03</text><rect x=\"479.2\" y=\"327.6\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"2.4\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>RM-10 Thickener: $8,100 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 494.1 344)\" x=\"494.1\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">RM-10</text><rect x=\"509.0\" y=\"327.8\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"2.2\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>SP-01 Disperser mechanical seal: $7,400 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 523.9 344)\" x=\"523.9\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\" font-weight=\"600\">SP-01</text><rect x=\"538.8\" y=\"328.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"2.0\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>SP-04 Pump diaphragm kit: $3,720 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 553.7 344)\" x=\"553.7\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">SP-04</text><rect x=\"568.6\" y=\"328.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"2.0\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>SP-06 Dispersion blade: $2,880 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 583.5 344)\" x=\"583.5\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">SP-06</text><rect x=\"598.4\" y=\"328.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"2.0\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"><title>SP-02 Filling line gasket set: $2,400 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 613.3 344)\" x=\"613.3\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\" font-weight=\"600\">SP-02</text><rect x=\"628.2\" y=\"328.0\" width=\"21.8\" height=\"2.0\" fill=\"#A9B2C0\"><title>SP-05 Drive belt: $1,300 a year, class C</title></rect><text transform=\"rotate(-45 643.1 344)\" x=\"643.1\" y=\"344\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#5A6475\">SP-05</text><line x1=\"58\" x2=\"654\" y1=\"330\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"#8A93A3\"/><text x=\"132.5\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\">A: 5 items, 79.5%</text><line x1=\"207.0\" x2=\"207.0\" y1=\"98\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"#8A93A3\"/><text x=\"213.0\" y=\"172.2\" fill=\"#26324A\">79.5%</text><text x=\"266.6\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\">B: 4 items, 15.1%</text><line x1=\"326.2\" x2=\"326.2\" y1=\"98\" y2=\"330\" stroke=\"#8A93A3\"/><text x=\"332.2\" y=\"138.1\" fill=\"#26324A\">94.7%</text><text x=\"490.1\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\">C: 11 items, 5.3%</text><polyline points=\"72.9,259.4 102.7,225.7 132.5,199.3 162.3,174.2 192.1,150.2 221.9,137.8 251.7,127.2 281.5,120.5 311.3,116.1 341.1,112.7 370.9,109.6 400.7,108.4 430.5,107.4 460.3,106.4 490.1,105.7 519.9,105.0 549.7,104.6 579.5,104.3 609.3,104.1 639.1,104.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0B2A5A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"72.9\" cy=\"259.4\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-01: cumulative 31.2%</title></circle><circle cx=\"102.7\" cy=\"225.7\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-02: cumulative 46.1%</title></circle><circle cx=\"132.5\" cy=\"199.3\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-03: cumulative 57.9%</title></circle><circle cx=\"162.3\" cy=\"174.2\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>PK-01: cumulative 69.0%</title></circle><circle cx=\"192.1\" cy=\"150.2\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-04: cumulative 79.5%</title></circle><circle cx=\"221.9\" cy=\"137.8\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-05: cumulative 85.0%</title></circle><circle cx=\"251.7\" cy=\"127.2\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>PK-02: cumulative 89.7%</title></circle><circle cx=\"281.5\" cy=\"120.5\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-06: cumulative 92.7%</title></circle><circle cx=\"311.3\" cy=\"116.1\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-07: cumulative 94.7%</title></circle><circle cx=\"341.1\" cy=\"112.7\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>PK-04: cumulative 96.2%</title></circle><circle cx=\"370.9\" cy=\"109.6\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-08: cumulative 97.5%</title></circle><circle cx=\"400.7\" cy=\"108.4\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-09: cumulative 98.1%</title></circle><circle cx=\"430.5\" cy=\"107.4\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>SP-03: cumulative 98.5%</title></circle><circle cx=\"460.3\" cy=\"106.4\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>PK-03: cumulative 98.9%</title></circle><circle cx=\"490.1\" cy=\"105.7\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>RM-10: cumulative 99.3%</title></circle><circle cx=\"519.9\" cy=\"105.0\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>SP-01: cumulative 99.6%</title></circle><circle cx=\"549.7\" cy=\"104.6\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>SP-04: cumulative 99.7%</title></circle><circle cx=\"579.5\" cy=\"104.3\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>SP-06: cumulative 99.8%</title></circle><circle cx=\"609.3\" cy=\"104.1\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>SP-02: cumulative 99.9%</title></circle><circle cx=\"639.1\" cy=\"104.0\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#0B2A5A\"><title>SP-05: cumulative 100.0%</title></circle><line x1=\"370.9\" x2=\"370.9\" y1=\"228\" y2=\"310.0\" stroke=\"#0B6FA4\" stroke-opacity=\".6\"/><circle cx=\"370.9\" cy=\"314.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"/><text x=\"390.9\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\">RM-08 dispersant</text><text x=\"390.9\" y=\"221\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$33,600 a year</text><line x1=\"519.9\" x2=\"519.9\" y1=\"266\" y2=\"317.8\" stroke=\"#0B6FA4\" stroke-opacity=\".6\"/><circle cx=\"519.9\" cy=\"321.8\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"/><text x=\"539.9\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\">SP-01 mechanical seal</text><text x=\"539.9\" y=\"259\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$7,400 a year</text><line x1=\"609.3\" x2=\"609.3\" y1=\"304\" y2=\"318.0\" stroke=\"#0B6FA4\" stroke-opacity=\".6\"/><circle cx=\"609.3\" cy=\"322.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\"/><text x=\"629.3\" y=\"282\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#0B6FA4\">SP-02 gasket set</text><text x=\"629.3\" y=\"297\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5A6475\">$2,400 a year</text></svg><figcaption>Illustrative data for a fictional manufacturer: 20 purchased items, 12 months of consumption.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Three of the six are A items: epoxy resin, titanium dioxide and hardener. Value-based ABC already gives them attention. The other three are buried in class C:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>RM-08 Dispersant additive</strong>, $33,600 a year. Every batch needs it, it comes from a single supplier, and the lead time is eight weeks.</li>\n<li><strong>SP-01 Disperser mechanical seal</strong>, $7,400 a year. The plant uses about four a year, and a replacement takes ten weeks to arrive.</li>\n<li><strong>SP-02 Filling line gasket set</strong>, $2,400 a year. The $40 part from the opening paragraph.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Together these three are worth $43,400 a year, under 2% of the total. Managed as ordinary C items, they would be counted once a year and reordered when someone noticed the bin was empty.</p>\n<p>The ranking misleads in the other direction too. All six spare parts fall in class C, with a combined value of $28,500. A value-only view says spares do not matter. Any maintenance manager will tell you otherwise.</p>\n<h2>Add a criticality rating</h2>\n<p>The fix is a second label on every item. Ask three questions: if we ran out today, would a line stop? Is there a substitute or a second supplier? How long would it take to get more?</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Rating</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Meaning</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">1. Vital</td><td>Production stops. There is no substitute, and resupply takes weeks.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">2. Essential</td><td>Production is disrupted, but a substitute, second supplier or workaround is available within days.</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">3. Desirable</td><td>No effect on output. Available locally the same day or week.</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Production and maintenance staff should set these ratings, not purchasing alone. They know which parts have no workaround.</p>\n<p>The two labels together decide the control policy. Value sets how tightly you manage the item; criticality sets how much protection it gets.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Class</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Vital (1)</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Essential (2)</th><th style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Desirable (3)</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><strong>A</strong></td><td>Tight control and protected supply: forecast-driven orders, a supply agreement or second source, high service level</td><td>Tight control with lean stock: frequent orders, no excess buffer</td><td>Tight control with minimum stock: buy close to need</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><strong>B</strong></td><td>Standard reorder point with a raised service level</td><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">Standard reorder point</td><td>Standard reorder point with a lower service level</td></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><strong>C</strong></td><td>Never run out: hold a generous fixed minimum and check it on a schedule</td><td>Simple min/max or two-bin</td><td>Buy on demand, or hold a token quantity</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>What changes at Ridgeline</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The three vital C items get protection.</strong> Two spare mechanical seals on the shelf cost $3,700 and ten gasket sets cost $400. A three-month minimum of dispersant, 600 kg, costs $8,400. That is $12,500 in total to cover three items that can each stop the plant.</li>\n<li><strong>The non-vital A items get leaner.</strong> Xylene and steel pails are high in value but available from several local suppliers. They need frequent orders and close tracking, not a large buffer.</li>\n<li><strong>The vital A items get both.</strong> Epoxy resin, titanium dioxide and hardener are expensive and irreplaceable. These justify supply agreements, a qualified second source and the careful safety stock calculation covered in <a href=\"safety-stock-for-manufacturers.html\">the next post</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Pitfalls specific to manufacturers</h2>\n<p><strong>One year is too short for spare parts.</strong> A seal that fails every three years shows zero usage in most years. Use three to five years of history for spares, and never delete a vital part because it did not move last year.</p>\n<p><strong>Shelf life caps the buffer.</strong> \"Hold plenty of the cheap items\" works for gaskets. It does not work for a catalyst or additive with a six-month shelf life. Set the maximum stock below what you will use before it expires.</p>\n<p><strong>History misleads when the product mix is changing.</strong> Raw material usage follows the production plan. If you are launching a product or dropping one, rank materials on planned usage for the next 12 months, not on the last 12.</p>\n<p><strong>Dead stock is invisible to ABC.</strong> The analysis ranks by usage, so an item with stock on the shelf and no usage never appears. Run a separate report of items with no movement in 12 months.</p>\n<p><strong>Report by pool.</strong> A single list is fine for ranking. For review meetings, show raw materials, packaging and spares separately, because different people own each one.</p>\n<p><strong>Re-rate after equipment changes.</strong> A new filling line or a decommissioned mixer changes which spares are vital. Review criticality whenever the equipment list changes, and at least once a year.</p>\n<h2>Your checklist</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>List purchased items by pool: raw materials, packaging, spare parts</li>\n<li>Pull 12 months of consumption for materials, and three to five years for spares</li>\n<li>Run the ABC ranking by annual value</li>\n<li>Rate every item for criticality with production and maintenance</li>\n<li>Flag every vital item in class C and set a fixed minimum for it</li>\n<li>Check shelf life before raising any buffer</li>\n<li>Run a no-movement report for dead stock</li>\n</ul>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/css/download.css\"><div class=\"j-dl-box\"><div><strong>Free Excel template</strong><span>The workbook for this series includes the Ridgeline example, with a criticality column and the combined policy for each item.</span></div><a class=\"btn\" href=\"../assets/downloads/Chmltech_Inventory_ABC_SafetyStock_Template.xlsx\" data-dl download>Download template</a></div>\n<p><strong>Next in the series:</strong> <a href=\"safety-stock-for-manufacturers.html\">Post&nbsp;4</a> sets safety stock for a manufacturer, where raw material demand comes from the production schedule and spare parts need a different method altogether.</p>\n<p><em>Chmltech Ltd. helps small and mid-sized businesses improve operations and adopt digital tools. If you would like help applying this to your own inventory, <a href=\"../contact.html\">get in touch</a>.</em></p>\n<dialog class=\"j-dialog\" id=\"dl\" aria-labelledby=\"dl-title\" data-file=\"../assets/downloads/Chmltech_Inventory_ABC_SafetyStock_Template.xlsx\" data-fname=\"Chmltech_Inventory_ABC_SafetyStock_Template.xlsx\" data-title=\"Inventory ABC and Safety Stock Template (Excel)\" data-ref=\"Inventory template\">\n  <form method=\"dialog\" class=\"form j-dl-form\" novalidate>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"j-dl-close\" aria-label=\"Close\">×</button>\n    <p class=\"eyebrow\">Chmlt